{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You shall not take vengeance.</b> Because anger overwhelms you; but about the Holy One, blessed be He, who overwhelms anger, it is written: 'נוקם ה׳ ובעל חימה' (a God of vengeance is YHWH and master of wrath)." "<b>And you shall not bear a grudge.</b> The verse speaks of monetary matters; but in bodily matters, he is not required to forgive him until he appeases him." "<b>You shall not take vengeance.</b> In deed. <b>And you shall not bear a grudge.</b> In thought." "<b>You shall not take vengeance.</b> Rashi explained: he said to him, 'Lend me your sickle,' etc. And if you ask: what is the difference that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not warn with a negative commandment against the one who refused to lend his fellow his vessels for no reason, but against this one, who has a great claim against him because he refused to lend him in the first place, He does warn with a negative commandment? One may answer: the first one did not lend him only because of stinginess, since his sickle was precious to him, and the Holy One, blessed be He, does not compel him to lend his vessels against his will. But this one, who would have lent him were it not for the hatred that moves him to take vengeance — if so, he is acting out of hatred; therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said: let the love you have for him overcome the hatred you have for him, and through this peace will come to the world." "<b>And you shall love your fellow as yourself.</b> If you do so, you will come to love him. The lamed in it is superfluous, as in: 'לכל חיל פרעה' (for all the army of Pharaoh), 'לכל כליו תעשה נחשת' (all its utensils you shall make of bronze). Another interpretation: it does not say ואהבת רעך כמוך, for it is impossible to do so; rather, <b>לרעך</b> — meaning: you shall love to do good for him just as you love that he do good for you. For 'what is hateful to you, do not do to your fellow.' And so you shall explain in the verse: 'and the stranger who dwells among you — ואהבת לו כמוך' (and you shall love him as yourself)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:34.239439131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}